rue\">×</span></button></div><div class=\"case-wrap\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">%%FIELD_f0377%%</p><h2 id=\"case-title-3\">%%FIELD_f0378%%</h2><p class=\"case-subtitle\">%%FIELD_f0379%%</p><dl class=\"case-meta\"><div><dt>%%FIELD_f0380%%</dt><dd>%%FIELD_f0381%%</dd></div><div><dt>%%FIELD_f0382%%</dt><dd>%%FIELD_f0383%%</dd></div><div><dt>%%FIELD_f0384%%</dt><dd>%%FIELD_f0385%%&amp;%%FIELD_f0386%%</dd></div></dl><figure class=\"case-figure\"><img src=\"%%FIELD_f0387%%\" alt=\"%%FIELD_f0388%%\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>%%FIELD_f0389%%</figcaption></figure>%%GALLERY_3%%<div class=\"case-sections\"><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0390%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0391%%&#x27;%%FIELD_f0392%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0393%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0394%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0395%%&amp;%%FIELD_f0396%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0397%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0398%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0399%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0400%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0401%%&#x27;%%FIELD_f0402%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0403%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0404%%</p></div></section></div><div class=\"case-bottom\"><a class=\"button dark\" href=\"#contact\" data-case-contact>%%FIELD_f0405%%<span>↗</span></a><a href=\"#project-4\" data-project=\"4\" class=\"text-link\">%%FIELD_f0406%%</a></div></div><div class=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></dialog><dialog class=\"case-dialog\" id=\"project-4\" aria-labelledby=\"case-title-4\"><div class=\"dialog-nav\"><span>%%FIELD_f0407%%<span class=\"desktop-label\">%%FIELD_f0408%%</span></span><button class=\"close-dialog\" aria-label=\"Close case study\">%%FIELD_f0409%%<span aria-hidden=\"true\">×</span></button></div><div class=\"case-wrap\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">%%FIELD_f0410%%</p><h2 id=\"case-title-4\">%%FIELD_f0411%%</h2><p class=\"case-subtitle\">%%FIELD_f0412%%</p><dl class=\"case-meta\"><div><dt>%%FIELD_f0413%%</dt><dd>%%FIELD_f0414%%</dd></div><div><dt>%%FIELD_f0415%%</dt><dd>%%FIELD_f0416%%</dd></div><div><dt>%%FIELD_f0417%%</dt><dd>%%FIELD_f0418%%</dd></div></dl><figure class=\"case-figure\"><img src=\"%%FIELD_f0419%%\" alt=\"%%FIELD_f0420%%\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>%%FIELD_f0421%%</figcaption></figure>%%GALLERY_4%%<div class=\"case-sections\"><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0422%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0423%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0424%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0425%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0426%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0427%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0428%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0429%%&#x27;%%FIELD_f0430%%</p></div></section><section class=\"case-section\"><h3>%%FIELD_f0431%%</h3><div><p>%%FIELD_f0432%%</p></div></section></div><div class=\"case-bottom\"><a class=\"button dark\" href=\"#contact\" data-case-contact>%%FIELD_f0433%%<span>↗</span></a><a href=\"#project-1\" data-project=\"1\" class=\"text-link\">%%FIELD_f0434%%</a></div></div><div class=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></dialog>\n<dialog id=\"gallery-dialog\" class=\"gallery-dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"gallery-title\"><div class=\"dialog-nav\"><span>%%FIELD_f0435%%</span><button class=\"close-dialog\" aria-label=\"Close work preview\">%%FIELD_f0436%%<span aria-hidden=\"true\">×</span></button></div><div class=\"gallery-dialog-content\"><p id=\"gallery-client\" class=\"eyebrow\"></p><h2 id=\"gallery-title\"></h2><img id=\"gallery-preview\" src=\"%%FIELD_f0437%%\" alt=\"%%FIELD_f0438%%\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\"><p class=\"gallery-disclaimer\">%%FIELD_f0439%%</p><a href=\"#contact\" data-case-contact class=\"button dark\">%%FIELD_f0440%%<span>↗</span></a></div><div class=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></dialog>\n<div class=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"portfolio-data\">{\"projects\": [{\"id\": 1, \"title\": \"The Quran Scholars Hub\", \"category\": \"Brand Identity\", \"description\": \"A complete visual identity developed from scratch for an educational institution focused on Quranic and Arabic studies.\", \"subtitle\": \"Brand Identity · Digital Design · Publication Design\", \"meta\": [{\"label\": \"Role\", \"value\": \"Sole Designer\"}, {\"label\": \"Duration\", \"value\": \"5 Months\"}, {\"label\": \"Type\", \"value\": \"Educational Institution\"}], \"sections\": [{\"title\": \"Overview\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The Quran Scholars Hub is an educational institution focused on Quranic and Arabic studies. The project involved building its visual presence from the ground up, including its brand identity, digital communication, and publications. I worked as the sole designer throughout, developing the visual system and applying it across multiple touchpoints.\"]}, {\"title\": \"The Challenge\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The biggest challenge was creating a complete identity from scratch while establishing consistency across different areas of the institution's communication. With limited initial branding direction, the project required developing a clear visual language and maintaining it across social media, publications, and other brand applications.\"]}, {\"title\": \"The Approach\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The identity was built around the institution's educational and Quranic purpose. The logo combines the Arabic letter ق (Qaf) — creating a direct visual connection with the word Quran — with an open book representing learning, reading, and Quranic education.\", \"Blue for trust & reliability. Gold for Islamic character & a premium feel.\", \"Trustworthy · Educational · Modern · Islamic · Premium\"]}, {\"title\": \"Brand System\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Logo · Color Palette · Typography · Brand Guidelines · Social Media · Publications · Book Covers\"]}, {\"title\": \"Publications\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The publication work required understanding the educational concepts first, then translating them into visuals that could appeal to children while maintaining a consistent brand identity. Illustrations, typography, colors, and visual structure were developed as part of the wider brand system.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Result\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The project gave The Quran Scholars Hub a proper and consistent digital presence , with a recognizable visual identity across its communication. The client response was extremely positive, and the work developed into a long-term design relationship.\", \"Portfolio assets: Logo · Brand Identity · Brand Guidelines · Color Palette · Book Covers\", \"Actual book copies are not included in the portfolio because the publication copyrights belong to the client.\"]}]}, {\"id\": 2, \"title\": \"Journey to Jannah\", \"category\": \"Children's Islamic Educational Series\", \"description\": \"A four-level Islamic Studies book series designed to make learning more engaging, visual, and memorable for children.\", \"subtitle\": \"Children's Islamic Educational Book Series\", \"meta\": [{\"label\": \"Role\", \"value\": \"Complete Book Designer\"}, {\"label\": \"Duration\", \"value\": \"~4 Months\"}, {\"label\": \"Publications\", \"value\": \"Four-Level Series\"}], \"sections\": [{\"title\": \"Overview\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Journey to Jannah is a four-level Islamic Studies book series created for children, progressing through different learning levels. The goal was to make Islamic education more engaging and visually accessible while maintaining a consistent identity throughout the series. I handled the complete design — from covers and layouts to interior pages, illustrations, and character development.\"]}, {\"title\": \"The Challenge\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Designing for children requires a careful balance: the books needed to communicate educational content clearly without becoming visually boring or overwhelming. Another major challenge was developing the illustration direction, creating the recurring character, and establishing a page layout that could work consistently across a multi-level series.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Design Direction\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Make learning visually engaging without compromising clarity.\", \"Colors, typography, illustrations, and visual storytelling were selected specifically to attract children and keep them engaged with the content.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Character System\", \"paragraphs\": [\"A recurring illustrated character was developed as part of the series. The character visually explains different concepts and gives the books a recognizable personality — maintained across all four levels to strengthen consistency. Its clothing colors were adapted across the different books, allowing each level its own variation while remaining clearly connected to the series.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Series Consistency\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Instead of completely redesigning every level, the core visual system remained consistent. Layouts stayed structured and spacious, while selected elements — colors, illustrations, character clothing — were adjusted between levels, creating enough variation to distinguish each publication while keeping the series visually connected.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Result\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The final outcome was a complete four-level book series, with covers, interior pages, layouts, illustrations, and a consistent visual system. The client responded very positively after seeing the completed publications.\"]}]}, {\"id\": 3, \"title\": \"The Path to the Arabic Language\", \"category\": \"Educational Editorial Design\", \"description\": \"A collection of Arabic-learning publications designed around readability, typography, consistency, and structured learning.\", \"subtitle\": \"Educational Editorial Design\", \"meta\": [{\"label\": \"Role\", \"value\": \"Complete Book Designer\"}, {\"label\": \"Duration\", \"value\": \"~1.5 Months\"}, {\"label\": \"Audience\", \"value\": \"UK & US Learners\"}], \"sections\": [{\"title\": \"Overview\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The Path to the Arabic Language is an educational publication project developed for The Quran Scholars Hub's international audience, including two publications: Arabic Conversations , a practical book built around everyday dialogue, and Arabic Grammar , a structured publication covering foundational through advanced concepts.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Design Direction\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Unlike Journey to Jannah, these publications were designed for relatively older learners. The approach was intentionally minimal, professional, and easy to read — focused on typography, structure, readability, consistency, and color rather than unnecessary visual complexity.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Color & Branding\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The original Quran Scholars Hub brand colors were integrated into the publications, maintaining visual consistency with the wider institution while giving the books a professional and attractive appearance.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Typography\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Typography was kept deliberately minimal, making the information easy to read and understand without distracting visual elements. For the Conversations publication in particular, the design let the dialogue and educational content remain the primary visual focus.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Arabic Typography\", \"paragraphs\": [\"One of the most demanding aspects of the project was working with Arabic text — careful attention to letterforms, spacing, harakat, i'raab, text fitting, and readability. Organizing Arabic content within fixed design spaces while maintaining accuracy and readability became a key part of the process.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Result\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The final publications provided a clean, structured, and consistent visual system for Arabic learning. The client responded very positively and highly appreciated the finished work.\"]}]}, {\"id\": 4, \"title\": \"The Broken Egoist\", \"category\": \"Biographical Book Design\", \"description\": \"A complete biographical book design combining editorial structure, typography, storytelling, and a distinctive Urdu literary element.\", \"subtitle\": \"Biographical Book Design\", \"meta\": [{\"label\": \"Role\", \"value\": \"Complete Book Designer\"}, {\"label\": \"Duration\", \"value\": \"~1 Month\"}, {\"label\": \"Type\", \"value\": \"Personal Client Project\"}], \"sections\": [{\"title\": \"Overview\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The Broken Egoist is a biographical book based on a real-life story. The project was commissioned through a personal client connection and required the complete visual development of the book.\"]}, {\"title\": \"My Role\", \"paragraphs\": [\"Proofreading · Layout · Cover Design · Interior Design · Typography · Complete Book Formatting\"]}, {\"title\": \"The Approach\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The main focus was creating a consistent editorial flow that allowed the story to move naturally through the book. The design needed to support the narrative rather than compete with it, keeping the structure clear and the reading experience cohesive.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Unique Element\", \"paragraphs\": [\"One of the distinctive elements of the publication was an Urdu Ghazal included at the end of the book at the client's request — adding a literary dimension and requiring the visual treatment to transition naturally from the main narrative into the Urdu poetic section.\"]}, {\"title\": \"Result\", \"paragraphs\": [\"The complete book was designed and delivered to the client, including its cover, interior structure, typography, and final layout. The client response was exceptionally positive.\"]}]}], \"more\": [{\"title\": \"Certificates\", \"organization\": \"Association for Development & Law\", \"category\": \"branding\"}, {\"title\": \"Collaboration Posters\", \"organization\": \"Association for Development & Law\", \"category\": \"branding\"}, {\"title\": \"Organizational Designs\", \"organization\": \"Association for Development & Law\", \"category\": \"branding\"}, {\"title\": \"Invitation Cards\", \"organization\": \"University & Club Work\", \"category\": \"editorial\"}, {\"title\": \"Event Graphics\", \"organization\": \"University & Club Work\", \"category\": \"editorial\"}, {\"title\": \"Posters\", \"organization\": \"Association for Development & Law\", \"category\": \"editorial\"}, {\"title\": \"Social Media Posts\", \"organization\": \"University & Club Work\", \"category\": \"digital\"}, {\"title\": \"Promotional Designs\", \"organization\": \"University & Club Work\", \"category\": \"digital\"}, {\"title\": \"Campaign Graphics\", \"organization\": \"Association for Development & Law\", \"category\": \"digital\"}, {\"title\": \"Event Admission Posters\", \"organization\": \"University & Club Work\", \"category\": \"campaigns\"}, {\"title\": \"Sports Posters\", \"organization\": \"University & Club Work\", \"category\": \"campaigns\"}], \"services\": [{\"title\": \"Brand Identity\", \"description\": \"I create distinctive and consistent visual identities that give brands a clear visual voice and a strong foundation for communication.\", \"tags\": \"Logo Design · Visual Identity · Brand Systems · Brand Guidelines\"}, {\"title\": \"Editorial & Book Design\", \"description\": \"I design books and publications with strong hierarchy, typography, structure, and visual consistency — from individual covers to complete publication systems.\", \"tags\": \"Book Design · Book Covers · Educational Publications · Complete Layout · Typography\"}, {\"title\": \"Digital & Social Media Design\", \"description\": \"I create engaging visual content for digital platforms, helping organizations and brands communicate clearly and consistently online.\", \"tags\": \"Social Media · Digital Campaigns · Marketing Graphics · Digital Content\"}, {\"title\": \"Packaging Design\", \"description\": \"I develop packaging visuals that combine clear communication, strong branding, and an appealing presentation.\", \"tags\": \"Packaging Graphics · Product Presentation · Brand Integration\"}, {\"title\": \"Marketing & Print Design\", \"description\": \"I turn information, campaigns, and ideas into clear visual communication designed for both digital and print applications.\", \"tags\": \"Posters · Advertising · Promotional Materials · Business Cards · Invitations · Certificates\"}, {\"title\": \"Thumbnail Design\", \"description\": \"I create attention-focused thumbnails designed to communicate the subject quickly and make digital content visually engaging.\", \"tags\": \"YouTube · Video Content · Digital Media\"}], \"experience\": [{\"year\": \"2024\", \"role\": \"Graphic Designer\", \"organization\": \"Dept. of Criminology, Islamia University of Bahawalpur — Part-time\", \"description\": \"Grew public awareness campaign reach by 60% designing infographics, event collateral, and marketing materials for 10+ departmental initiatives. Produced publication-ready visual data presentations for 4 criminology research projects and delivered 100% of assigned work on schedule.\"}, {\"year\": \"2025\", \"role\": \"Media Director\", \"organization\": \"Association for Development & Law — Part-time, Hybrid\", \"description\": \"Designed a unified visual communication system — posters, banners, social media graphics — rolled out across all ADL chapters, lifting event attendance by 28%. Built a reusable brand identity system and template library for the South Punjab chapter, cutting ad-hoc design requests by 50%.\"}, {\"year\": \"Now\", \"role\": \"Freelance Graphic Designer\", \"organization\": \"Upwork — Remote, Full-time\", \"description\": \"Scaled visual brand identity for 20+ international clients with a 4.9★ satisfaction rating, delivering branding, logo design, and social media graphics within 48-hour turnaround. Drove a 35% average engagement lift through targeted print and digital assets, and streamlined revision cycles by 40% with structured creative briefs and standardised file delivery.\"}], \"about\": [\"I started with almost no formal design knowledge. I began by exploring Canva, experimenting with different types of designs, and gradually discovering tools like Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, and other creative software.\", \"I never followed one fixed course or stayed limited to one tool. Whenever something felt difficult, I learned what I needed, explored new possibilities, and kept improving through practical work.\", \"Today, after nearly two years in graphic design, I've worked with around 20 local clients and contributed to projects for international organizations and NGOs.\", \"My work spans branding, editorial design, educational publications, social media, and digital communication.\"], \"otherServices\": [\"Logo Design\", \"Branding\", \"Social Media Posts\", \"Poster Design\", \"Book Cover Design\", \"Complete Book Layout\", \"Packaging Design\", \"Business Cards\", \"Invitations\", \"Certificates\", \"Marketing Graphics\", \"Custom Projects\"], \"tools\": [\"Canva Pro\", \"Photoshop\", \"Illustrator\", \"InDesign\", \"Premiere Pro\"], \"philosophy\": \"Every project begins with understanding. I don't believe in designing simply for the sake of making something visually attractive. I look at the purpose behind the project, the audience it needs to reach, and the problem the design needs to solve. From there, I build a visual direction, choose the right tools and resources, and develop the design with consistency and attention to detail.\", \"approach\": \"What does the client actually need? I first understand the objective, then identify what resources I have, what information or assets I need from the client, and what can make the final design more effective or distinctive.\"}</script>\n<script>\n(() => {\n  'use strict';\n  const $ = (q, root = document) => root.querySelector(q);\n  const $$ = (q, root = document) => [...root.querySelectorAll(q)];\n  const data = JSON.parse($('#portfolio-data').textContent);\n  const motionQuery = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');\n  let paused = motionQuery.matches;\n  const motionButton = $('#motion-toggle');\n  function setMotion(value) {\n    paused = value;\n    document.documentElement.classList.toggle('motion-paused', paused);\n    motionButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(paused));\n    motionButton.innerHTML = paused ? 'Enable motion <span aria-hidden=\"true\">▶</span>' : 'Pause motion <span aria-hidden=\"true\">Ⅱ</span>';\n    if (paused) $$('.cursor').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('visible'));\n  }\n  setMotion(paused);\n  motionButton.addEventListener('click', () => setMotion(!paused));\n  motionQuery.addEventListener('change', e => setMotion(e.matches));\n\n  // The entrance runs before page content in intro-controller.\n\n  // Content is visible by default; only opt into reveal effects when supported.\n  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window && !paused) {\n    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {\n      entries.forEach(entry => { if (entry.isIntersecting) { entry.target.classList.add('visible'); observer.unobserve(entry.target); } });\n    }, {threshold:.06, rootMargin:'0px 0px 45px 0px'});\n    $$('.reveal').forEach(e => observer.observe(e));\n    document.documentElement.classList.add('animate-ready');\n  }\n\n  const menu = $('#mobile-nav');\n  const menuButton = $('.menu-toggle');\n  function setMenu(open) {\n    menu.hidden = !open;\n    menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));\n    menuButton.setAttribute('aria-label', open ? 'Close menu' : 'Open menu');\n  }\n  menuButton.addEventListener('click', () => setMenu(menu.hidden));\n  $$('a', menu).forEach(a => a.addEventListener('click', () => setMenu(false)));\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === 'Escape' && !menu.hidden) { setMenu(false); menuButton.focus(); } });\n  document.addEventListener('click', e => { if (!menu.hidden && !menu.contains(e.target) && !menuButton.contains(e.target)) setMenu(false); });\n  matchMedia('(min-width:901px)').addEventListener('change', e => { if (e.matches) setMenu(false); });\n\n  let lastProjectTrigger = null;\n  let activeDialog = null;\n  let returnHash = '#work';\n  function showDialog(dialog, trigger) {\n    if (!dialog) return;\n    if (activeDialog === dialog) return;\n    if (!activeDialog) { lastProjectTrigger = trigger || document.activeElement; returnHash = location.hash.startsWith('#project-') ? '#work' : (location.hash || '#work'); }\n    if (activeDialog) activeDialog.close();\n    activeDialog = dialog;\n    document.body.classList.add('dialog-open');\n    dialog.showModal();\n    dialog.scrollTop = 0;\n    $('.close-dialog', dialog).focus({preventScroll:true});\n    $$('.cursor').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('visible'));\n  }\n  function closeDialog({restoreHash = true, restoreFocus = true} = {}) {\n    if (!activeDialog) return;\n    activeDialog.close();\n    activeDialog = null;\n    document.body.classList.remove('dialog-open');\n    if (restoreHash) history.replaceState(null, '', returnHash);\n    if (restoreFocus && lastProjectTrigger?.isConnected) lastProjectTrigger.focus({preventScroll:true});\n  }\n  $$('[data-project]').forEach(link => link.addEventListener('click', e => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    const id = link.dataset.project;\n    const wasOpen = !!activeDialog;\n    showDialog($(`#project-${id}`), link);\n    if (wasOpen) history.replaceState(null, '', `#project-${id}`);\n    else history.pushState(null, '', `#project-${id}`);\n  }));\n  $$('.close-dialog').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => closeDialog()));\n  $$('dialog').forEach(dialog => dialog.addEventListener('cancel', e => { e.preventDefault(); closeDialog(); }));\n  function syncProjectHash() {\n    const id = /^#project-([1-4])$/.exec(location.hash)?.[1];\n    if (id) showDialog($(`#project-${id}`));\n    else if (activeDialog) closeDialog({restoreHash:false});\n  }\n  addEventListener('popstate', syncProjectHash);\n  addEventListener('hashchange', syncProjectHash);\n  syncProjectHash();\n  $$('[data-case-contact]').forEach(a => a.addEventListener('click', e => {\n    e.preventDefault(); closeDialog({restoreHash:false,restoreFocus:false});\n    history.replaceState(null, '', '#contact');\n    $('#contact').scrollIntoView({behavior:paused?'instant':'smooth'});\n    setTimeout(() => $('#project-form input').focus({preventScroll:true}), paused ? 0 : 450);\n  }));\n\n  $$('.filter').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {\n    $$('.filter').forEach(b => { const selected = b === button; b.classList.toggle('active', selected); b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(selected)); });\n    let count = 0;\n    $$('.gallery-card').forEach(card => {\n      const show = button.dataset.filter === 'all' || card.dataset.category === button.dataset.filter;\n      card.hidden = !show;\n      if (show) { count++; card.classList.add('visible'); }\n    });\n    $('#filter-status').textContent = `${count} work items shown.`;\n  }));\n  $$('[data-more]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {\n    const card = button.closest('.gallery-card');\n    const item = {title: $('h3', card).textContent, organization: $('.gallery-organization', card).textContent};\n    $('#gallery-title').textContent = item.title;\n    $('#gallery-client').textContent = item.organization;\n    $('#gallery-preview').src = $('img', button).getAttribute('src');\n    $('#gallery-preview').alt = `Illustrative preview for ${item.title}; original artwork to be added`;\n    showDialog($('#gallery-dialog'), button);\n  }));\n  $$('[data-service]').forEach(a => a.addEventListener('click', () => { $('#project-service').value = a.dataset.service; }));\n\n  $('#copy-email').addEventListener('click', async () => {\n    try {\n      await navigator.clipboard.writeText('%%CONTACT_email%%');\n      $('#copy-status').textContent = 'Email address copied.';\n    } catch {\n      $('#copy-status').textContent = 'Select the address above to copy it, or click it to email me.';\n    }\n  });\n  $('#project-form').addEventListener('submit', e => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    const form = e.currentTarget;\n    if (!form.reportValidity()) return;\n    const values = new FormData(form);\n    const topic = values.get('service') || 'Design project';\n    const body = `Hi Taha,\\n\\n${values.get('message')}\\n\\nProject type: ${topic}\\nBudget / timeline: ${values.get('timeline') || 'To discuss'}\\n\\nName: ${values.get('name')}\\nEmail: ${values.get('email')}`;\n    const uri = `https://wa.me/%%CONTACT_whatsapp%%?text=${encodeURIComponent(body)}`;\n    const status = $('#form-status');\n    status.hidden = false;\n    status.textContent = 'Your project brief is ready in WhatsApp. Review it and tap Send. You can also reach me on WhatsApp at %%CONTACT_displayNumber%%.';\n    window.location.href = uri;\n  });\n\n  // Keep the native pointer. A light trailing ring is an enhancement for precise pointing devices only.\n  const finePointer = matchMedia('(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)');\n  const cursors = $$('.cursor');\n  let targetX = 0, targetY = 0, x = 0, y = 0, frame = 0, initialized = false;\n  function renderCursor() {\n    x += (targetX - x) * .24; y += (targetY - y) * .24;\n    cursors.forEach(c => c.style.transform = `translate3d(${x}px,${y}px,0) translate(-50%,-50%)`);\n    if (Math.abs(targetX-x) + Math.abs(targetY-y) > .2) frame = requestAnimationFrame(renderCursor);\n    else frame = 0;\n  }\n  document.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {\n    if (paused || !finePointer.matches || e.pointerType !== 'mouse') return;\n    targetX=e.clientX;targetY=e.clientY;\n    if (!initialized) { x=targetX;y=targetY;initialized=true; }\n    const onControl = !!e.target.closest('a,button,summary');\n    const onBlue = !!e.target.closest('.about-section,.contact-section,.process-section,.site-footer');\n    const onField = !!e.target.closest('input,textarea,select');\n    cursors.forEach(c => { c.classList.toggle('visible', !onField); c.classList.toggle('hovering', onControl); c.classList.toggle('on-blue', onBlue); });\n    if (!frame) frame=requestAnimationFrame(renderCursor);\n  }, {passive:true});\n  document.documentElement.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => cursors.forEach(c => c.classList.remove('visible')));\n  addEventListener('blur', () => cursors.forEach(c => c.classList.remove('visible')));\n})();\n\n// Match the mobile menu to the header's actual height, including text zoom.\n(() => {\n  const header = document.querySelector('.site-header');\n  const update = () => document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--header-height', `${header.getBoundingClientRect().height}px`);\n  update();\n  if ('ResizeObserver' in window) new ResizeObserver(update).observe(header);\n  else window.addEventListener('resize', update);\n})();\n\n</script>\n</body></html>"